-Each chunk is rendered as a collection of points using `GL_POINTS`, with vertex attributes for position, normal, and texture coordinates. It binds the chunk VAO, sets model/view/projection matrices, and calls `glDrawArrays(GL_POINTS, 0, num_vertices)`. A pitfall is that meshes are always updated on the GPU even if empty to prevent floating quads when destroying blocks near chunk borders.
